WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.030
A speech to save a local park begins:

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.010
"Can we really let
our park fall apart?

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.550
" Nobody in the hall shouts back.

4
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.070
Nobody is meant to.

5
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:14.110
So why would a writer ask a
question that wants no answer?

6
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.970
And why might a speech that uses
this trick ten times work less

7
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.030
well?

8
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.470
In this mission, you'll slide
between formal and informal

9
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:23.120
writing.

10
00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:26.220
You'll use Standard English
when a task needs it.

11
00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:30.330
You'll learn persuasive
techniques that spell a forest.

12
00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.910
And you'll squeeze a long
sentence into a short summary.

13
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.150
Your mission: find out why a
question with no answer can be so

14
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.540
persuasive.
